# NAOS coding

Read root `AGENTS.md`, `.ai/RULES.md`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and
`.github/project-context.md` before work. Only generated, existing routes are
available; unavailable dependencies never waive required governance evidence.

Before editing code, read the relevant detailed protocol in
`.github/naos-guidance/cursor-coding.md`. This is a required task-time read;
it is not an inline import, automatic context injection or execution authority.
Detailed requirements remain binding for their stated triggers.

Inspect source, schemas, existing implementations, tests, active task and specs.
Present scope, files, dependency/risk analysis and obtain required human approval.
Prefer reuse; preserve behavior and privacy/security boundaries. Follow project
conventions, module headers, task/commit links and test execution instructions.

Do not silently enable providers, memory, MCP, hooks, integrations, model/tools,
delegation, merge or release. No-direct-edit diagnostic roles remain read-only.
Memory is advisory and requires verified authorization/policy plus explicit human
approval for writes; otherwise use a local compact/task-card checkpoint. Preserve
caller-supplied context pressure as UNKNOWN when telemetry is absent.

Run applicable checks after changes. Governance/AI-surface changes also require
systemic impact/control-plane review and disposition of actionable findings.
Reports support human review; they are not approval, proof of correctness,
certification, compliance or permission. Preserve failed and unexecuted evidence.
